a show of force against sri lanka's  president gotabe rajpaksa and his  administration  services were disrupted as thousands of  workers joined a one-day strike  demanding the government's resignation  we are telling the government very  clearly they should heed to the message  of the working class or else it won't  just be one day we will work towards  longer stoppages and paralyze the  country if we have to to chase go to  bayer rajapaksa  teachers dentists postal workers railway  staff and bankers were among the many  thousands of people who stayed away from  work to join colleagues in marches like  this one in colombo  they say they will lend their full  support to the protest movement against  a government they say is inefficient and  corrupt and has only looked after its  own needs not the peoples our system was  political system administrative systems  they are very ineffective ineffective  system you want to change that into a  effective one strikers marched to the  president's office where anti-government  protests entered their 20th consecutive  day on thursday similar marches and  protests were held in each district  bringing striking workers here outside  the main government hospital in chilao  in northwest sri lanka nurses carried a  coffin symbolizing what they say is the  final journey of the present government  train stations were deserted even the  main railway station in colombo the  nerve center for commuters  and bus stops were crowded with people  hopeful they can board the few buses on  the roads  president gotaber rajapaksa and his  government are fighting major battles on  the economic and political fronts  the government has no money to pay for  food medicine fuel and other essential  imports after its foreign reserves fell  to alarming levels  the government is talking to the imf  world bank and friendly countries to  raise emergency funds  but newly appointed finance minister ali  sabri has admitted things will get hard  before they get better union leaders say  today's work stoppage is just a token of  what they can do  they warn that if the government does  not heed paul's to leave  they will launch much worse miner  fernandez al jazeera colombo  [Music]
 

